{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_exceeded_3.march","start_line":10,"start_col":2,"end_line":13,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileWrite` (reached from `main`: main → save). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileWrite` does not raise it.\nhelp: add a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.","code":"cap_grant_exceeded","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":10,"start_col":30,"end_line":10,"end_col":30,"text":", _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite)","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
